0168069c-90b4-4867-aca1-f48cdad49281	a1b2c3d4-e5f6-4789-8123-456789abcdef	assistant	The available internal document excerpts are from **“SAS Healthcare Data.pdf”** and appear to cover part of a chapter or section on creating healthcare reports using SAS Enterprise Guide.\n\n## Key information available\n\n### 1. The document includes a reporting workflow for healthcare data\nThe table-of-contents excerpts show sections on identifying appropriate professional claims, creating outreach reports, creating internal reports, and automating reports with macro variables [Source 5]. The surrounding chapter also includes subsections such as extracting code from Enterprise Guide tasks, import data code, query builder code, and automate code [Source 1], [Source 2].\n\n### 2. The “Create Internal Report” section focuses on children’s primary-care visits\nThe available detailed section explains how to build an internal report of **children who have had at least one primary care–related professional visit in the past year** [Source 3]. The report is intended for healthcare workers at **Healthy Living, Inc.** to help ensure that members are receiving appropriate care [Source 3].\n\n### 3. The report is built using SAS Enterprise Guide Query Builder\nThe instructions specify using **Query Builder** from **Tasks → Data** [Source 3]. The user is directed to select two data sources: **CurrentMemberKids** and **ProfessionalVisits** [Source 3].\n\n### 4. The output query and table names are specified\nThe query should be named **“Most Recent Visits-Kids”**, and the output table should be **WORK.KidsVisits** [Source 3].\n\n### 5. The report retrieves the most recent professional visit per child\nThe selected fields include **DOB** and **Age** from `CurrentMemberKids`, and **MemberID** and **BeginDos** from `ProfessionalVisits` [Source 3]. For `BeginDos`, the instructions specify using the **MAX** summary option so that the query retrieves the most recent visit for each child [Source 3].\n\n## Limitation\n\nOnly a small portion of the document was retrieved. The excerpts identify broader sections—such as outreach reporting and macro-based automation—but do not provide enough detail to fully summarize those topics beyond their presence in the document [Source 1], [Source 5].	[{"document_name": "SAS Healthcare Data.pdf", "page_number": 73, "content": "Create Internal Report ............................................................................................................... 71 \\nCase Study: Automating Reports with Macro Variables .............................................73 \\nExtract Code from Enterprise Guide Tasks ...................", "score": 0.005028237123042345}, {"document_name": "SAS Healthcare Data.pdf", "page_number": 85, "content": "Create Internal Report  \\nThis section shows you how to build a report of children who have had at least one primary care\\u2013related \\nprofessional visit in the past year. This report is used by healthcare workers in Healthy Living, Inc., to ensure \\nthat members are receiving appropriate care. \\n1. Select", "score": 0.001979420892894268}, {"document_name": "SAS Healthcare Data.pdf", "page_number": 5, "content": "Identify Appropriate Professional Claims ............................................................................................. 68 \\nCreate Outreach Report ......................................................................................................................... 70 \\nCreate Inter", "score": 0.00022484944202005863}]	2026-11-09 05:35:48.099258+00
