28e2c79f-02ef-4890-b332-40ea19d86489	2a5c3412-b5c3-4458-bd9d-7b470ad223fb	assistant	Regression analysis is a statistical method used to study and model the relationship between a **response variable**—the outcome you want to explain or predict—and one or more **predictor variables**—the inputs used to explain or predict that outcome.\n\nIn **simple linear regression**, the goal is to use one predictor variable to:\n\n- assess whether the predictor significantly explains variation in the response variable, and\n- predict response values from predictor values [Source 2].\n\nA regression model also separates the variation in the data into:\n\n- **Model variation**: variability explained by the regression model,\n- **Error variation**: variability not explained by the model,\n- **Total variation**: overall variability in the data [Source 1].\n\nRegression can be used for several purposes, including **prediction**, **variable screening**, **model specification**, and **parameter estimation** [Source 3]. In predictive use, the main focus is building a model that predicts future values of the response variable as a function of the predictor variables [Source 3].	[{"document_name": "Statistics-I-Introduction-to-Anova-Regression-And-Logistic.pdf", "page_number": 159, "content": "3-36 Chapter 3  Regression  \\n  \\nThe Analysis of Variance (ANOV A) table provides an analysis of the variability observed in the data and \\nthe variability explained by the regression line. \\n                                      Analysis of Variance \\n \\n                                             Sum ", "score": 0.9443230032920837}, {"document_name": "Statistics-I-Introduction-to-Anova-Regression-And-Logistic.pdf", "page_number": 151, "content": "3-28 Chapter 3  Regression  \\n  \\n33\\nSimple Linear Regression Analysis\\nThe objectives of simple linear regression are to\\n\\u0084 assess the significance of the predictor variable in \\nexplaining the variability or behavior of the \\nresponse variable\\n\\u0084 predict the values of the response variable given \\nthe val", "score": 0.9202483892440796}, {"document_name": "Statistics-I-Introduction-to-Anova-Regression-And-Logistic.pdf", "page_number": 174, "content": "ranging from simple to complex, you will focus on applications for analytical studies and predictive \\nmodeling. Other SAS procedures are better suited for analyzing experimental data. \\nThe distinction between using multiple regression for an analytic analysis and prediction modeling is \\nsomewhat art", "score": 0.8904577493667603}]	2026-11-09 12:13:07.165802+00
